  "label": "Stereotype: Unarmed Black Youth as Threat",
  "description": "The phrase 'unarmed black youth' is a loaded reference to real-world incidents and media narratives that have historically portrayed Black youth as a threat, even when they are not armed. This stereotype is used to frame the officers' actions as justified, despite the context of the quote being extreme and violent.",
